  The duplicate component is a bug fix: that discrimination was never real.
  The menopause component is a deliberate narrowing — removing younger,
  denser, still-cycling women takes away easy negatives, so a lower AUC on a
  harder and more clinically relevant cohort is the expected cost, not a loss.
